{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f9ec83ae71e27974d0a9ec3996bdd95034ea7b0f8c2dd2ee20ac5c182322d68b","digest":{"component_or_area":"Config-read gate (scripts/check_config_reads.py)","key_entities":["scripts/check_config_reads.py","_collect_reads","check_config_reads.py::_collect_reads","_config_schema.py","config.py","CodeHealthConfig.enabled","CodeHealthConfig.analyzers","McpConfig.readonly","McpConfig.allow_llm","McpConfig.allow_jira_sync","JiraConfig.allow_insecure","ReconcilerConfig.allow_insecure","VerifyConfig.require_plan_review_for_close","ReconcilerConfig.lock_lease_secs","tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py","tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","mcp_server.py","_mcp_gate","JiraConfig.__post_init__"],"problem_keywords":["config read gate","false negatives","attribute name matching","global scope","inert fields","dataclass resolution"],"propositions":["The gate matches field names globally as bare terminal attribute names rather than resolving reads to their owning dataclass, causing same-named fields on unrelated configs to satisfy each other.","Common reused field names like 'enabled', 'path', 'timeout' bypass the gate's check because any read of that bare name anywhere in src/rebar passes all fields named it, regardless of class ownership.","A field is satisfied only when its receiver expression resolves to the dataclass declaring it, not when a same-named attribute exists elsewhere.","Four live config fields newly flag when the gate is fixed: McpConfig.readonly, McpConfig.allow_llm, McpConfig.allow_jira_sync, and JiraConfig.allow_insecure; each requires a factual # read-via: marker documenting its actual reader.","Existing # read-via: markers must be audited to report any pointer naming a closed rebar ticket id, preventing expired markers from persisting silently."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787871594091646001,"uuid":"1c056abc-de67-4db0-ab1a-aeab3ac6d07f"}